  "topic": "syslog Function",
  "explanation": "The syslog function is used in C programming to send messages to the system logger, which records events, errors, or informational messages. It is particularly useful in system-level applications for logging activities that can be monitored externally, aiding in debugging, auditing, and system management.",
  "syntax": "syslog(int priority, const char *format, ...)",
  "code_example": [
    "#include <syslog.h>",
    "",
    "int main() {",
    "    openlog(\"example_program\", LOG_PID, LOG_USER);",
